---
import { worksiteScene } from "@intentic/site-content/worksite";
import DocsLayout from "../../components/docs/DocsLayout.astro";
import DocsRelated from "../../components/docs/DocsRelated.astro";
import WorksiteFigure from "../../components/figures/WorksiteFigure.astro";

/* THE MENTAL MODEL, not a feature list. Four nouns every later page spends without introducing. */

const scene = worksiteScene;

/* The practical payoff of the picture: the same four parts, as the thing a reader actually decides to add. */
const reaches = [
    {
        want: "Your agents are slow, or you want the work off your laptop",
        add: "A different machine",
        because: "Compute is the only thing it decides. Moving is a switch, not a migration: the workspace keeps its address and its name.",
    },
    {
        want: "Two jobs should not see each other's code, tools or credentials",
        add: "Another sandbox",
        because: "A separate container and separate volumes on the same machine. Nothing crosses between them.",
    },
    {
        want: "The same sandbox should work differently on a certain kind of task",
        add: "Another persona",
        because: "Same code, same tools installed, different set handed to the turn: other accounts, another folder, other instructions.",
    },
    {
        want: "There is more code for the agents already in there to work on",
        add: "Another project",
        because: "A repository in the workspace. Every conversation in that sandbox can reach it the moment it arrives.",
    },
];
---

<DocsLayout
    pageId="worksite"
    heading="The worksite"
    lead="Four words the rest of these docs spend as though you already had them: the machine, a sandbox, a persona, a project. This page is the one picture they all sit in, and the place each of them is defined."
>
    <h2>{scene.heading}</h2>
    <p>
        {scene.sub} A building camp is the useful shape to borrow, because the thing everyone already knows about a site is the thing that
        is actually true here: the ground decides nothing, the work is done by people who each carry their own tools and their own orders,
        and what goes up outlasts every shift that worked on it.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-embed my-8">
        <WorksiteFigure />
    </div>

    <h2>Which one do you reach for</h2>
    <p>
        Most questions about intentic are one of these four in disguise. The answer is usually the smallest part that changes: a persona
        before a sandbox, a sandbox before a machine.
    </p>
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>You want</th>
                <th>Add</th>
                <th>What that gets you</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            {
                reaches.map((row) => (
                    <tr>
                        <td>{row.want}</td>
                        <td>
                            <strong>{row.add}</strong>
                        </td>
                        <td>{row.because}</td>
                    </tr>
                ))
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
        The fork between the middle two is worth reading in full once you are running more than one job:{" "}
        <a href="/docs/autonomous-employees/#another-sandbox-or-another-persona">another sandbox, or another persona?</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Where the drawing stops being true</h2>
    <p>
        A picture that is never corrected turns into a belief. Four things about a building camp do not hold here, and each of them is a
        place readers otherwise guess wrong.
    </p>
    {
        scene.limits.map((limit) => (
            <Fragment>
                <h3>{limit.heading}</h3>
                <p>{limit.body}</p>
            </Fragment>
        ))
    }

    <DocsRelated
        links={[
            { href: "/docs/architecture/", title: "Architecture", why: "the same parts as a system map: where identity, code, state and compute actually live." },
            { href: "/docs/glossary/", title: "Glossary", why: "every other word these docs use as if you had it." },
            { href: "/where-it-runs/", title: "Where it runs", why: "the machine choice in full, including what it costs." },
            { href: "/docs/parallel-agents/", title: "Parallel agents", why: "what happens when several agents are put on one project at once." },
        ]}
    />
</DocsLayout>
